      "content": "so if the structure itself is rigged toward the big powers, then isn't the whole \"international law\" thing just a tool for hegemony? it seems like the argument for global governance basically ignores the fact that true sovereignty can't exist if you're constantly being managed by these supranational bodies. is there actually any legitimate case for this kind of system, or is it just fundamentally broken?",
